    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **James Wood** stands as our premier play with a 76.05 score, fueled by a favorable matchup against a vulnerable pitcher and a high-leverage leadoff spot. He is joined by **Tyler Soderstrom** (67.73) and **Josh Naylor** (66.05), both of whom benefit from positive park factors and favorable lineup placement. **Seiya Suzuki** also warrants strong consideration at 63.54; while the park is slightly detrimental, his proven BvP success against his opposing starter and his status as a primary catalyst in the two-hole make him a high-efficiency start for our Roto categories. We are particularly monitoring the wind conditions for **Cole Young**, as the breeze out to the outfield helps boost his base projection into \"Strong\" territory (55.02) despite the challenge of facing the high-velocity Roki Sasaki.\n\nThe bench decisions remain tight, with **Jose Caballero** serving as our most notable exclusion. While his baseline metrics are competitive, his lack of a confirmed spot in the lineup combined with a difficult matchup against an arm like Burke necessitates caution given our strict game-cap management. We are keeping a close watch on the lineups for **Dalton Rushing** and **Henry Bolte**; both possess decent scoring profiles, but their projected spots at the bottom of the order drag down their overall efficiency. We are also tracking **Vinnie Pasquantino** on the IL and ensuring our remaining depth\u2014including **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Max Muncy**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Travis Bazzana**\u2014remains ready should any late-hour lineup shifts or weather developments arise. With **Corbin Carroll** and **Mickey Moniak** sidelined by scheduling, the current configuration offers our best path to maximizing steals and production today.",
